repository-code: "https://github.com/<your-org>/jepx-epf-benchmark"
url: "https://github.com/<your-org>/jepx-epf-benchmark"
abstract: "Reproducibility package for a probabilistic 48-step electricity price forecasting benchmark on the Japan Electric Power Exchange (JEPX). Includes processed 30-min half-hourly price data for Tokyo and Kansai areas (2022-2023), Python pipeline implementing LEAR, DDNN-Normal, DDNN-Johnson-SU, N-HiTS, rolling Quantile Regression Averaging, and adaptive conformal prediction under the Lago 2021 rolling-window protocol, plus Diebold-Mariano and Hansen-Lunde-Nason Model Confidence Set statistical testing."
keywords:
  - electricity price forecasting
  - JEPX
  - probabilistic forecasting
  - LEAR
  - distributional neural networks
  - N-HiTS
  - quantile regression averaging
  - conformal prediction
  - Diebold-Mariano test
  - Model Confidence Set
  - Japan
  - renewable energy
